.page mcc 1 Marisa's C compiler
.alias cc

# SYNOPSIS
*mcc* [*-c*] [*-E*] [*-o* _FILE_] [*-I* _DIR_] [*-D* _NAME_[=_VALUE_]] [*-U* _NAME_] _FILE_...
*mcc* [*-nostdlib*] [*-s*] [*-M*] [*-l* _LIB_] [*-L* _DIR_] _FILE_.c _FILE_.o _FILE_.a ...
*mcc* *-fsyntax-only* | *--version* | *--help*

# DESCRIPTION
`mcc` is a C compiler that runs on TouhouOS and makes TouhouOS programs. It reads C11 source (without variable-length arrays and complex numbers), compiles it straight to x86-64 machine code, and links the result with `mld` into a static executable that starts like every other program of the system: crt0.o, your code, libgap, and whatever libraries you name. There is no assembler step and no temporary file; `cc` is the same program under a shorter name.

The compiler is small and simple on purpose: every expression is evaluated in a few registers with the operands kept on the stack, so the code is correct and readable rather than fast. It can compile itself (see /ScarletDevilMansion/src/mcc), and so it can compile much of the rest of the system: all of kappabox is built with it in the test suite.

Each _FILE_ ending in .c is compiled. Files ending in .o and .a are handed to the linker as they are. With *-c* only the objects are written (_FILE_.o next to where you are, or *-o* for a single file); without it the program is linked into `a.out` or the name given with *-o*, and its mode is set to executable.

# OPTIONS
@ *-c*
    Compile, do not link.
@ *-E*
    Preprocess only and write the tokens, one line per source line, to standard output (or to *-o*).
@ *-o* _FILE_
    Name of the output.
@ *-I* _DIR_
    Look for headers in _DIR_ first. *-isystem* _DIR_ adds a directory after those; *-nostdinc* leaves out the system directories.
@ *-D* _NAME_[=_VALUE_]
    Define a macro (the value is 1 if omitted). *-U* _NAME_ removes one, *-include* _FILE_ reads _FILE_ before the source.
@ *-l* _LIB_
    Link with the library libNAME.a, where NAME is the argument; it is searched for in the *-L* directories and then in the system lib directory. libgap (the C library, mathematics and pthreads together) is always linked; *-lm*, *-lpthread* and *-lc* are accepted and mean nothing. The graphics and sound libraries are *-lkappa*, *-lfairy*, *-laudio*, *-limg* and *-lz*.
@ *-nostdlib*
    No crt0.o and no libgap: the program brings its own _start.
@ *-s*
    Do not write a symbol table into the executable. *-M* prints a link map (the address of every symbol) to standard output.
@ *-fsyntax-only*
    Check the program and produce nothing.
@ *--version*, *--help*
    Who is speaking, and a summary of the options.

Options such as *-O2*, *-g*, *-Wall*, *-std=c11*, *-static*, *-pthread*, *-m64* and *-fPIC* are accepted so that existing command lines work, and they change nothing. *-S* is refused: mcc has no assembly text, it writes machine code. *-shared* is refused: TouhouOS has no dynamic linking.

# THE LANGUAGE
`mcc` understands C11 with these exceptions and additions.

- Integer types of 1, 2, 4 and 8 bytes, `_Bool`, enums, bit-fields, float and double. `long double` is a double.
- All declarators, structs, unions, anonymous members, flexible array members, designated and nested initializers, compound literals, statement expressions, case ranges, `typeof`, `_Generic`, `_Static_assert`, `_Alignas`, `_Alignof`, `__func__` and `_Thread_local`.
- Calls follow the System V AMD64 convention, so objects from clang link with mcc objects: arguments in registers, structs by value (up to 16 bytes in registers), variadic functions with a real `va_list`.
- The preprocessor has `#include_next`, `#pragma once`, `__COUNTER__`, `__VA_OPT__`, `, ## __VA_ARGS__` and `__has_include`. The predefined names include `__x86_64__`, `__STDC_VERSION__` (201112L), `__TOUHOU__` and `__MCC__`.
- `__builtin_va_*`, `__builtin_offsetof`, `__builtin_expect`, `__builtin_bswap*`, `__builtin_clz*`, `__builtin_ctz*`, `__builtin_popcount*`, `__builtin_thread_pointer`, `__atomic_*` and `__sync_*` are built in.
- `__attribute__`, `asm` labels and `register` are parsed; only `packed`, `aligned` and `weak` have an effect.
- Inline assembly uses the GNU syntax: outputs, inputs and clobbers, register, memory and immediate operands, the a/b/c/d/S/D constraints, matching operands and register variables (`register long r10 __asm__("r10")`). mcc has a small AT&T assembler built in for the integer instructions programs really use (mov, the ALU group, shifts, lea, push/pop, xchg, xadd, cmpxchg with lock, bsf/bsr/bswap/popcnt, setcc/cmovcc, jumps to numeric labels, rep movs/stos/lods/scas/cmps, syscall, cpuid, rdtsc, in/out). x87 and SSE instructions are not understood.
- Not supported: variable-length arrays, complex numbers, `alloca`, computed goto, K&R function definitions.

# FILES
@ /ScarletDevilMansion/include
    The headers of libgap and of the system libraries.
@ /ScarletDevilMansion/lib/mcc/include
    The freestanding headers that belong to the compiler: stddef.h, stdarg.h, stdint.h, limits.h, float.h, stdbool.h.
@ /ScarletDevilMansion/lib
    crt0.o, libgap.a and the other static libraries.
@ /ScarletDevilMansion/src/mcc
    The source of the compiler. *cd* there and run *mcc main.c -o mcc2*; the result is byte for byte the program that built it.

# ENVIRONMENT
@ MCC_ROOT
    Replaces /ScarletDevilMansion as the root of the include and lib directories.

# DIAGNOSTICS
A mistake is reported as `file:line: error: text`, followed by the source line, a caret and a remark from Marisa; compilation stops at the first error and no object is written. The plain text in front is the real message.

# EXIT STATUS
0 when everything was built, 1 after an error in the program, the options or the link.

# EXAMPLES
    mcc hello.c -o hello && ./hello
    mcc -O2 -Wall -c util.c main.c && mcc util.o main.o -lm -o tool
    mcc -E -DDEBUG=1 prog.c | less
    cd /ScarletDevilMansion/src/mcc && mcc main.c -o /tmp/mcc2

# SEE ALSO
mld(1), mar(1), gensokyo(7)
